00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.960
your thoughts about the film.

00:00:31.960 --> 00:00:35.930
Quick spoiler warning, I will be discussing
the end credit scenes in full, explaining

00:00:35.930 --> 00:00:40.480
their link to the rest of the movie as well
as talking connections to and potential speculation

00:00:40.480 --> 00:00:42.950
on Avengers: Infinity War.

00:00:42.950 --> 00:00:46.900
The mid-credits scene begins with T'Challa
attending the UN in Vienna and delivering

00:00:46.900 --> 00:00:49.320
a speech to the international community.

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:53.680
In the speech, T'Challa announces that, for
the first time in his country's history, he's

00:00:53.680 --> 00:00:57.250
opening up Wakanda to the world and offers
to share their knowledge and resources.

00:00:57.250 --> 00:01:02.410
Wakanda has, up until now, isolated itself,
using its technology to hide its precious

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:07.890
vibranium resources "in plain sight", but
at the UN, T'Challa implies that it's no longer

00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:11.300
right for Wakanda or any country to hide itself
way.

00:01:11.300 --> 00:01:15.909
In fact, he wants Wakanda to be an example
of how we should all treat each other, and

00:01:15.909 --> 00:01:21.630
as he says, "in times of crisis, the wise
build bridges while the foolish build barriers".

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:26.030
In response, one of the UN delegates asks
what Wakanda can offer the rest of the world,

00:01:26.030 --> 00:01:29.310
because in his eyes it's just a "nation of
farmers".

00:01:29.310 --> 00:01:33.310
The scene stops at this point, with Black
Panther, Nakia, and Everett Ross all smiling

00:01:33.310 --> 00:01:37.940
knowingly at the utter foolishness of that
question – and Ross perhaps recognises too

00:01:37.940 --> 00:01:42.240
just how wrong he was earlier in the film
when he shared that delegate's attitude.

00:01:42.240 --> 00:01:46.410
Still, we can assume that T'Challa would go
on to reveal that Wakanda has reserves of

00:01:46.410 --> 00:01:51.040
vibranium and has developed technology and
medical treatments beyond what is available

00:01:51.040 --> 00:01:53.350
anywhere else in the world.

00:01:53.350 --> 00:01:57.810
By taking this step, T'Challa has acted on
Nakia's very real concern that during her

00:01:57.810 --> 00:02:03.350
time as a Wakandan spy abroad she has "seen
too many in need to turn a blind eye."

00:02:03.350 --> 00:02:07.940
It's clear from the film that opening up access
to Wakandan medical technology, for instance,

00:02:07.940 --> 00:02:12.781
has the potential to revolutionise how people
recover from injuries as Everett Ross fully

00:02:12.781 --> 00:02:17.379
recovers from being shot in the spine in just
one day after being treated by Shuri.

00:02:17.379 --> 00:02:21.909
Access to Wakandan vibranium could be a double-edged
sword as although it will likely be useful

00:02:21.909 --> 00:02:26.129
in the fight against Thanos, once the secret's
out, it could attract other villains to try

00:02:26.129 --> 00:02:29.609
and get their hands on it, as was the case
with Ulysses Klaue.

00:02:29.609 --> 00:02:34.980
And, along with Thanos's search for the still-to-be-uncovered
Soul Stone, that could be another reason why

00:02:34.980 --> 00:02:39.129
we see in the Infinity War trailer that the
Mad Titan has sent his Outriders to invade

00:02:39.129 --> 00:02:40.159
the country.

00:02:40.159 --> 00:02:45.909
But this opening up of Wakanda also has huge
implications beyond Avengers: Infinity War

00:02:45.909 --> 00:02:50.939
as it means we're likely to see future Marvel
movies cross over with Black Panther and Wakanda.

00:02:50.939 --> 00:02:55.319
The world, characters, and tech of Wakanda
are so rich and ripe with opportunities for

00:02:55.319 --> 00:02:59.560
storytelling that it seems likely that Marvel
will want to incorporate Black Panther's world

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:01.510
wherever it fits.

00:03:01.510 --> 00:03:05.769
The mid-credits scene is also a call-back
to the UN Sokovia Accords meeting in Vienna

00:03:05.769 --> 00:03:10.980
in Captain America: Civil War where T'Challa's
father, King T'Chaka, addressed the UN and

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:15.310
attempted to make a similar speech offering
Wakandan co-operation and outreach to the

00:03:15.310 --> 00:03:16.639
wider world.

00:03:16.639 --> 00:03:20.760
T'Chaka was, of course, killed before he could
finish his speech when Zemo orchestrated an

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:24.209
attack on the UN building in order to frame
Bucky.

00:03:24.209 --> 00:03:28.510
And this takes us to Black Panther's second
and final post-credits scene that has an even

00:03:28.510 --> 00:03:31.719
more direct lead-in to Avengers: Infinity
War.

00:03:31.719 --> 00:03:36.120
In this scene, we find someone waking up in
a small hut in the Wakandan countryside surrounded

00:03:36.120 --> 00:03:38.099
by some inquisitive children.

00:03:38.099 --> 00:03:42.819
As the person steps outside, we discover it's
Bucky, who we last saw being put on ice in

00:03:42.819 --> 00:03:45.870
the mid-credits scene for Captain America:
Civil War.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.299
Bucky agreed to be put under so that Wakandan
scientists could figure out what was wrong

00:03:49.299 --> 00:03:54.279
with his mind, and in the Avengers: Infinity
War prelude comic, we learn that it's Shuri

00:03:54.279 --> 00:03:59.909
who's figured out how to remove trigger words
that HYDRA inserted in Bucky's mental programming.

00:03:59.909 --> 00:04:03.699
Shuri's treatment appears to have worked as
Bucky seems calm and well.

00:04:03.699 --> 00:04:07.729
He's also wearing a blue sling around his
missing arm in the scene and at the end Shuri

00:04:07.729 --> 00:04:12.230
tells him to come with her as there is "much
more for [him] to learn", which likely means

00:04:12.230 --> 00:04:16.510
they need to update him on what's been happening
since he was in cryo-stasis and get him back

00:04:16.510 --> 00:04:18.160
in full shape.

00:04:18.160 --> 00:04:22.240
We know from the Avengers: Infinity War trailer
that Bucky has his missing arm restored at

00:04:22.240 --> 00:04:26.440
some point, so Shuri probably still has some
more work to do on that and perhaps it'll

00:04:26.440 --> 00:04:28.670
be made of vibranium too.

00:04:28.670 --> 00:04:32.910
There's also a big hint to what Bucky's role
might be next in the name "White Wolf" which

00:04:32.910 --> 00:04:35.450
the children in the scene call out as they
run off.

00:04:35.450 --> 00:04:39.550
"White Wolf" is an interesting Marvel easter
egg and a nod to the Black Panther comic-book

00:04:39.550 --> 00:04:44.920
character Hunter who was adopted by T'Challa's
father T'Chaka when his parents crash-landed

00:04:44.920 --> 00:04:46.090
in Wakanda.

00:04:46.090 --> 00:04:50.720
The white foreigner, Hunter, aka White Wolf,
loved his adoptive country and eventually

00:04:50.720 --> 00:04:53.000
became head of the secret police in Wakanda.

00:04:53.000 --> 00:04:57.860
So, in this post-credits scene Marvel could
be alluding to the MCU's Bucky taking on a

00:04:57.860 --> 00:05:01.620
similar type of security role in Wakanda in
the future.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:05.270
Indeed, in the Avengers: Infinity War trailer,
Bucky looks like he might be heading up a

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:08.260
group of Wakandan warriors on the battlefield.

00:05:08.260 --> 00:05:13.530
And given his past activities, it would be
a natural fit for Bucky to take on black ops-style

00:05:13.530 --> 00:05:15.890
missions on behalf of Black Panther.

00:05:15.890 --> 00:05:20.810
Wakanda already operates a network of spies,
or War Dogs as they're called, and perhaps

00:05:20.810 --> 00:05:24.980
Bucky could join them, maybe teaming up with
Nakia on future missions.

00:05:24.980 --> 00:05:28.990
It'll be interesting to see if Bucky does
take on the new identity of White Wolf, leaving

00:05:28.990 --> 00:05:33.280
behind his former alter ego of the Winter
Soldier, or whether this is just simply a

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:35.420
nice nod to the comics.

00:05:35.420 --> 00:05:39.580
By the way, given the importance of Shuri's
tech genius, I want to point out another way

00:05:39.580 --> 00:05:42.930
in which this could link in to the next Avengers
team-up.

00:05:42.930 --> 00:05:47.050
We know that Thanos pursues Vision in the
Infinity War movie and that the Mad Titan's

00:05:47.050 --> 00:05:51.860
Black Order are seen either attempting to
extract or manipulate the Mind Stone in Vision's

00:05:51.860 --> 00:05:52.860
forehead.

00:05:52.860 --> 00:05:57.070
And it's been rumoured that Vision gets taken
to Wakanda in the film so Shuri can extract

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.640
the Mind Stone from him and keep it safe.

00:05:59.640 --> 00:06:03.700
In the Avengers: Infinity War prelude comic
Shuri boasts that the tech she's developed

00:06:03.700 --> 00:06:09.420
surpasses anything Tony Stark has done, specifically
how Stark created Ultron, which seems like

00:06:09.420 --> 00:06:13.480
another big hint that Shuri could be involved
in removing the Mind Stone from Vision and

00:06:13.480 --> 00:06:15.870
keeping him alive at the same time.

